commenders; HBS prefers one be a current or former supervisor. Recommenders answer two prompts (how the applicant compares to other well-qualified people in similar roles; most important constructive feedback given). Due at application deadline with 48-hour grace period for recommenders only.", "source_url": "https://www.hbs.edu/mba/blog/answering-your-questions-about-the-hbs-mba-application"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Joint degree applicants indicate it in the ''Start Application'' section of the HBS application; separate application and independent admission by the partner school.", "source_url": "https://apply.hbs.edu/www/documents/HBS%20MBA%20Application%20Guide%202026-2027.pdf"}, "notes": "Apply to HLS and HBS separately; each admits independently. Test, English, and recommendation entries are the general HBS MBA rules; joint pages themselves do not restate them."}'::jsonb,null,null),
('Harvard Business School','MBA/DMD (HBS + Harvard School of Dental Medicine)','mba','full-time','Not stated','Fall 2027 (assumed to follow the MBA cycle; not stated)','https://www.hbs.edu/mba/academic-experience/joint-degree-programs/harvard-school-of-dental-medicine','{"deadlines": {"value": "Joint degree pages give no dates; HBS Class of 2029 MBA rounds: Sept 9, 2026 and Jan 5, 2027 (12:00 PM ET).", "source_url": "https://www.hbs.edu/mba/admissions/application-dates"}, "application_fee": null, "tests": {"value": "Must take GRE or GMAT before applying; no preference between them; no GMAT/GRE waivers; if multiple scores are submitted only the highest single sitting is considered; unofficial scores accepted at submission, official scores must be sent to HBS. Executive Assessment not mentioned on pages read. No minimum score stated.", "source_url": "https://www.hbs.edu/mba/blog/answering-your-questions-about-the-hbs-mba-application"}, "english": {"ielts_min": "No minimum to apply; Admissions Board discourages below 7.5", "toefl_min": "No minimum to apply; discouraged below 109 iBT (or 5 on the 1-6 scale)", "duolingo": "accepted (no minimum to apply; discouraged below 145)", "pte_min": "No minimum to apply; discouraged below 75", "other_tests": null, "waiver": "Test required unless undergraduate institution''s sole language of instruction was English; if a graduate degree was taught in English, a test is recommended but not required", "source_url": "https://www.hbs.edu/mba/admissions/application-process/international-applicants"}, "essays": null, "video_assessment": null, "interview": {"value": "Apply to HBS and HSDM separately. HBS general process: interview by invitation only, 30 minutes with an MBA Admissions Board member, on campus, in hub cities or via Zoom; written reflection due within 24 hours after the interview. (General HBS MBA page; joint-degree page does not describe interviews.)", "source_url": "https://www.hbs.edu/mba/admissions/application-process"}, "recommendations": {"value": "Two recommenders; HBS prefers one be a current or former supervisor. Recommenders answer two prompts (how the applicant compares to other well-qualified people in similar roles; most important constructive feedback given). Due at application deadline with 48-hour grace period for recommenders only.", "source_url": "https://www.hbs.edu/mba/blog/answering-your-questions-about-the-hbs-mba-application"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Joint degree applicants indicate it in the ''Start Application'' section of the HBS application; separate application and independent admission by the partner school.", "source_url": "https://apply.hbs.edu/www/documents/HBS%20MBA%20Application%20Guide%202026-2027.pdf"}, "notes": "Established 2009; apply to both schools separately; current first- or second-year HSDM DMD students can apply to HBS in either round. Test, English, and recommendation entries are the general HBS MBA rules; joint pages themselves do not restate them."}'::jsonb,null,null),
('Stanford GSB','MBA','mba','full-time','2 years','Fall 2027 (2026-27 cycle; start date not stated on page read)','https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/mba','{"deadlines": {"value": "2026-27 cycle, all 4:00 PM PT: Round 1 Sep 9, 2026 (decision Dec 9, 2026); Round 2 Jan 6, 2027 (decision Apr 1, 2027); Round 3 Apr 7, 2027 (decision May 27, 2027). Deferred enrollment may apply in any round.", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/mba/admission/deadlines"}, "application_fee": {"value": "USD 275, nonrefundable. Reduced fee USD 100 for defer-eligible applicants (degree conferred Oct 1, 2026 to Sep 30, 2027); military waiver; need-based waiver (request by Dec 18, 2026).", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/mba/admission/application/fee"}, "tests": {"value": "GMAT or GRE required of all MBA applicants; no minimum score and no preference between tests; report one score from a single sitting (no superscoring); for 2026-27, if score expires before June 1, 2027 send official scores at submission. Executive Assessment accepted for MSx only.", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/mba/admission/application/application-essentials"}, "english": {"ielts_min": "7.0 overall (Academic)", "toefl_min": "iBT 100 for tests before Jan 21, 2026; page lists 5.0 (new scale) from Jan 21, 2026; paper-delivered test generally 75 total", "duolingo": "not stated", "pte_min": "68 overall (Academic); online PTE not accepted", "other_tests": null, "waiver": "Not required if undergraduate or graduate degree was taught exclusively in English (explain in Additional Information if university is in a non-English-primary country; committee may still ask for a test). Citizenship and work experience do not exempt. Required if undergrad was taught in whole or part in another language unless a later graduate degree was entirely in English.", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/mba/admission/application/test-scores/english-language-proficiency"}, "essays": {"items": [{"prompt": "What matters most to you, and why?", "limit": "650 words", "required": true}, {"prompt": "Why Stanford for you?", "limit": "350 words", "required": true}, {"prompt": "How will you enhance the MSx community? (joint MBA/MSx applicants only)", "limit": "350 words", "required": false}], "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/mba/admission/application/application-essentials"}, "video_assessment": {"value": "No video assessment or video essay is listed among the MBA application components (education, GMAT/GRE, activities, work experience, resume, recommendations, two essays). The application-process page says the office will not review supplemental materials such as video links. (Absence-based: the pages do not state ''no video'' in those words.)", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/mba/admission/application-process"}, "interview": {"value": "By invitation only after application review; valid test score required; every admitted candidate must interview. Structured behavioral interview with alumni volunteer or MBA admissions staff; remote or in person (no on-campus requests). Round 1 interviews mid-Sep to mid-Nov, Round 2 mid-Jan to mid-Mar, Round 3 mid-Apr to mid-May.", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/mba/admission/interviews"}, "recommendations": {"value": "Two letters required. First from current direct supervisor (alternatives if unavailable); second from another person who has supervised you; both from same organization allowed. Not family or direct reports; recommender must be sole author; letters in English (original plus English translation with translator contact if written in another language).", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/mba/admission/application/letters-recommendation"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "US bachelor''s degree or equivalent; unofficial transcripts at application (official only if admitted); resume (letter or A4, achievement-focused); professional experience section; personal info, activities and awards; optional short answers; Additional Information section. No minimum work experience stated; no preferred industry. Deferred-enrollment applicants list internships and part-time work.", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/mba/admission/application/application-essentials"}, "notes": "Duolingo is not listed among accepted tests on the Stanford English page; treat as not accepted unless Stanford confirms. Optional short-answer questions exist (page not read in detail). Credential: international degree must be equivalent to a US bachelor''s (see Education page, not read). Intake stated as fall 2027 based on 2026-27 cycle; start date not explicit."}'::jsonb,'{"class_label": "Class of 2027 (data as of 17 Sept 2025); Class of 2028 not found", "gmat_avg": 738, "gmat_median": null, "gmat_range": "540-780 (low-high, GMAT Classic)", "gmat_focus_median": null, "gmat_focus_range": "615-785 (low-high); average 689", "gre_verbal_avg": 164, "gre_quant_avg": 164, "gre_range": null, "gpa_avg": 3.76, "gpa_range": null, "work_exp_avg_years": 5.3, "work_exp_range": null, "class_size": 434, "international_pct": 38, "women_pct": 45, "countries": 64, "pct_submitted_gre": 44, "source_url": "https://www.clearadmit.com/2025/11/stanford-gsb-mba-class-of-2027-profile/", "source_name": "Clear Admit summary (official GSB page did not render numbers); 58% submitted GMAT"}'::jsonb,'{"report_label": "Class of 2025 employment report (full-time hires, 3 months after graduation)", "employed_3_months_pct": 81, "median_base_salary": "USD 185,000", "mean_base_salary": "USD 190,901", "top_industries": "Technology 35%, Finance 33%, Consulting 11%, Healthcare 5%, Energy 4%; 16% of class pursued own ventures", "top_employers": null, "international_employed_note": "90% had offers and 81% had accepted within 3 months (81% is the accepted figure). No international breakdown found.", "source_url": "https://poetsandquants.com/2025/12/16/stanford-mba-jobs-gsbers-total-pay-declines-for-a-2nd-straight-year/ ; https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/mba/career-impact/positions-compensation", "source_name": "Poets&Quants; Stanford GSB employment outcomes page (confirms 90%/81%)"}'::jsonb),
('Stanford GSB','MSx (Master of Science in Management, Stanford Sloan)','masters','full-time','12 months (1 year)','2027 (start date not stated; 2026-27 cycle)','https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/msx','{"deadlines": {"value": "2026-27, 4:00 PM PT: Round 1 Oct 8, 2026 (notification Dec 9, 2026); Round 2 Jan 6, 2027 (Apr 1, 2027); Round 3 Feb 11, 2027 (Apr 1, 2027). Joint MBA/MSx: Round 2 only.", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/msx/admission/deadlines"}, "application_fee": {"value": "USD 275 (stated on MSx deadlines page)", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/msx/admission/deadlines"}, "tests": {"value": "GMAT, GRE, or Executive Assessment required; no preference; no test waivers; take before submitting; online versions accepted; no averaging (one sitting). Minimums and validity not stated on page. Joint MBA/MSx applicants must submit GMAT or GRE.", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/msx/admission/application-requirements/test-scores"}, "english": {"ielts_min": "7.0 overall (Academic)", "toefl_min": "iBT 100 for tests before Jan 21, 2026; page lists 5 for later tests (appears to be new 1-6 scale)", "duolingo": "not stated", "pte_min": "68 overall (Academic)", "other_tests": null, "waiver": "Exempt if university taught all classes exclusively in English (undergraduate or graduate); citizenship/work experience do not exempt; may still be asked to test if the university is in a non-English-primary country.", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/msx/admission/application-requirements/test-scores/english-proficiency-tests"}, "essays": {"items": [{"prompt": "What matters most to you, and why?", "limit": "650 words", "required": true}, {"prompt": "How do you plan to support and enhance the experience of your classmates and the learning community at Stanford GSB?", "limit": "350 words", "required": true}, {"prompt": "How will the Stanford MSx Program, along with your experiences, skills, and network, help you achieve your career goals? (Career Aspirations short answer)", "limit": "not stated", "required": true}, {"prompt": "Why Stanford for You? Describe your aspirations and how your Stanford MSx experience will help you realize them. (joint MBA/MSx applicants only)", "limit": "350 words", "required": false}, {"prompt": "Optional short answers (up to three): a time in the past five years you created a significant impact", "limit": "1,200 characters each", "required": false}], "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/msx/admission/application-requirements/essays"}, "video_assessment": null, "interview": {"value": "By invitation only after written application review; valid test score required; virtual, about 45 minutes, in English, with an MSx admissions officer; all admits interview.", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/msx/admission/interviews"}, "recommendations": {"value": "Two letters, preferably from individuals who have supervised your work.", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/msx/admission/application-requirements"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "At least 8 years of post-graduate professional work experience (median 13+). Resume of max 2 pages, no photo; per-employer details (organization, revenue, title, salary, accomplishment, reason for leaving). Education, personal information/activities/awards sections.", "source_url": "https://www.gsb.stanford.edu/programs/msx/admission/application-requirements/professional-experience"}, "notes": "Mid-career program: 8-year minimum experience means Octavia (about 5 years consulting plus earlier roles) should check eligibility. Duolingo not mentioned on English page. MSx TOEFL new-scale line appears as ''5'' on the page."}'::jsonb,null,null),
