?", "limit": "350 words", "required": true}, {"prompt": "Reapplicant essay: how you have reflected and grown since your previous application, with relevant updates to your candidacy.", "limit": "250 words", "required": false}, {"prompt": "Additional information: share any additional information about yourself that cannot be found elsewhere in your application (may address extenuating circumstances).", "limit": "500 words", "required": false}], "source_url": "https://mba.wharton.upenn.edu/mba-application-requirements/"}, "video_assessment": {"value": "Page does not mention a video requirement.", "source_url": "https://mba.wharton.upenn.edu/mba-application-requirements/"}, "interview": {"value": "By invitation only. Round 1 invitations Oct 28, 2026; Round 2 Feb 19, 2027; Round 3 Apr 16, 2027. Carey JD/MBA and Lauder invitees also complete a Wharton Team-Based Discussion plus a program interview.", "source_url": "https://mba.wharton.upenn.edu/applying/"}, "recommendations": {"value": "One letter, preferably from a current or former supervisor, using GMAC Common Letter of Recommendation. Carey JD/MBA applicants submit two letters.", "source_url": "https://mba.wharton.upenn.edu/mba-application-requirements/"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Must be admitted to both Wharton MBA and the Penn Engineering (SEAS) program; considered dual-degree students only after both admissions confirmed. Engineering-side requirements not read.", "source_url": "https://mba.wharton.upenn.edu/wharton-engineering-dual-degree-program/"}, "notes": "Wharton-side requirements from the MBA requirements page; Penn Engineering side not covered."}'::jsonb,null,null),
('Wharton','Dr. Bruce I. Jacobs Master of Science in Quantitative Finance (MSQF)','masters','full-time','1 additional year after accelerated undergraduate path (STEM-certified master''s)','2027 cycle','https://jacobs-msqf.wharton.upenn.edu/','{"deadlines": {"value": "2027 Application Cycle: opens Aug 3, 2026; deadline Jan 5, 2027; interview invitations Jan 19, 2027; decisions Feb 11, 2027; enrollment deadline Feb 26, 2027.", "source_url": "https://jacobs-msqf.wharton.upenn.edu/admissions/"}, "application_fee": null, "tests": {"value": "GRE or GMAT optional in academic year 2026-2027, but will be required in future years.", "source_url": "https://jacobs-msqf.wharton.upenn.edu/admissions/"}, "english": null, "essays": {"items": [{"prompt": "Propose a potential idea for your practicum (quant finance research question, type of company to collaborate with, what you hope to learn).", "limit": "300 words", "required": true}], "source_url": "https://jacobs-msqf.wharton.upenn.edu/admissions/"}, "video_assessment": {"value": "One short one-way video interview response.", "source_url": "https://jacobs-msqf.wharton.upenn.edu/admissions/"}, "interview": {"value": "Invitation-only; in-person group discussion about 35 minutes with 5-6 applicants.", "source_url": "https://jacobs-msqf.wharton.upenn.edu/admissions/"}, "recommendations": {"value": "One letter, preferably a current or recent professor or research advisor.", "source_url": "https://jacobs-msqf.wharton.upenn.edu/admissions/"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "One-page resume; transcripts from every university with credit; Advisor Acknowledgement Form; eligibility limited to current Penn undergraduates in third year (second year for transfers); prerequisites MATH 2200 or ESE 2030, FNCE 1000, ACCT 1010.", "source_url": "https://jacobs-msqf.wharton.upenn.edu/admissions/"}, "notes": "Open only to current Penn undergraduates, so effectively not available to external international applicants. Application fee and English test policy not stated on page."}'::jsonb,null,null),
('Chicago Booth','Full-Time MBA','mba','full-time','21 months','2026-27 cycle (rounds Sep 2026 to Apr 2027); start term not named on page','https://www.chicagobooth.edu/mba/full-time','{"deadlines": {"value": "2026-27: Round 1 Sep 15, 2026 (decision Dec 3, 2026); Round 2 Jan 7, 2027 (Mar 25, 2027); Round 3 Apr 1, 2027 (May 20, 2027); Chicago Booth Scholars Apr 1, 2027. All 11:59 pm CT.", "source_url": "https://www.chicagobooth.edu/mba/full-time/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "application_fee": {"value": "USD 250, due at submission", "source_url": "https://www.chicagobooth.edu/mba/full-time/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "tests": {"value": "GMAT/GRE policy: page says ''All valid test scores are accepted''; self-report at application, official after admission; valid within five years; no superscores; no minimum stated. UChicago undergrads/grads may treat as optional.", "source_url": "https://www.chicagobooth.edu/mba/full-time/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "english": {"ielts_min": "7.0 (academic)", "toefl_min": "5.0 on the new scale (on/post Jan 21, 2026); 104 iBT (pre Jan 21, 2026); 600 paper", "duolingo": "accepted (min 135)", "pte_min": "70 (PTE Academic)", "other_tests": null, "waiver": "Candidates ''may be required'' to submit; the international page mentions no waivers, but the how-to-apply/requirements pages say waivers exist for citizens/permanent residents of English-official countries, graduates of English-instruction institutions, and 2+ years of full-time US residence and work. Below-minimum applicants may still apply, contingent on demonstrated English proficiency at interview.", "source_url": "https://www.chicagobooth.edu/mba/full-time/admissions/international-students"}, "essays": {"items": [{"prompt": "What is your immediate post-MBA career goal?", "limit": "300 characters", "required": true}, {"prompt": "What is your long-term post-MBA career goal?", "limit": "300 characters", "required": true}, {"prompt": "Upload an image and explain its significance to you.", "limit": "300 characters", "required": true}, {"prompt": "Share a fun fact or something unique about yourself.", "limit": "300 characters", "required": true}, {"prompt": "Is there any unclear information in your application that needs further explanation or additional details you would like to share with the Admissions Committee?", "limit": "300 words", "required": false}, {"prompt": "Reapplicants: Upon reflection, how has your perspective regarding your future, Chicago Booth, and/or getting an MBA changed since the time of your last application?", "limit": "300 words", "required": true}], "source_url": "https://www.chicagobooth.edu/mba/full-time/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "video_assessment": {"value": "Invited interviewees complete a recorded video simulation exercise (no video essay).", "source_url": "https://www.chicagobooth.edu/mba/full-time/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "interview": {"value": "Invitation-only, virtual, one interview with a current student or other Booth community member; required for admission.", "source_url": "https://www.chicagobooth.edu/mba/full-time/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "recommendations": {"value": "One letter from a supervisor (preferably current), submitted online; recommenders complete a skills assessment and two questions.", "source_url": "https://www.chicagobooth.edu/mba/full-time/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Resume; unofficial transcripts from all postsecondary institutions (official after admission); 4-year US bachelor''s equivalent (3-year international degrees considered); no minimum GPA, test score or work experience.", "source_url": "https://www.chicagobooth.edu/mba/full-time/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "notes": "Third-party credential evaluation not mentioned. F-1/J-1 visa documents requested after admission (diplomas, English test results, proof of financial resources). English scores valid 2 years, one test session only, no MyBest."}'::jsonb,'{"class_label": "Class of 2027 (entering fall 2025); 