ly"}, "video_assessment": {"value": "Two required videos, each max 90 seconds, single take, no editing: Q1 who you are, where you come from, what shaped you; Q2 randomly generated open-ended question, no prep.", "source_url": "https://mitsloan.mit.edu/mba/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "interview": {"value": "Required, by invitation only; virtual, scheduled in Eastern Time (one-on-one, about 30 minutes per FAQ).", "source_url": "https://mitsloan.mit.edu/mba/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "recommendations": {"value": "One recommendation letter (professional, ideally manager/supervisor; no family) plus two additional professional references different from the recommender.", "source_url": "https://mitsloan.mit.edu/mba/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "One-page resume (Times New Roman 10pt); scanned transcripts from all institutions (non-English: original plus certified translation); four-year degree or three-year non-US equivalent by matriculation; up to three work entries with compensation. Average about five years work experience, no formal minimum (FAQ).", "source_url": "https://mitsloan.mit.edu/mba/admissions/how-to-apply"}, "notes": "Three-year non-US bachelor''s accepted. GPA need not be converted. No credential evaluation requirement described; certified translation needed for non-English transcripts (WES acceptable). International students can get loans without US cosigner and are eligible for fellowships (FAQ). Visa requirements not stated on fetched pages. Cover letter is the only standing written essay."}'::jsonb,'{"class_label": "MBA Class of 2028 (entering fall 2026); GPA figure is a median, not an average", "gmat_avg": null, "gmat_median": null, "gmat_range": null, "gmat_focus_median": 675, "gmat_focus_range": "middle 80%: 645-715 (GMAT Focus)", "gre_verbal_avg": null, "gre_quant_avg": null, "gre_range": "Quant middle 80%: 160-170 (verbal not reported)", "gpa_avg": null, "gpa_range": "median 3.74 (4.0 scale); range not reported", "work_e