usive Leadership skills (situation, actions, outcome).", "limit": "250 words", "required": true}, {"prompt": "Essay 3: why Columbia Business School is a good academic, cultural and professional fit, with specific detail.", "limit": "250 words", "required": true}, {"prompt": "Optional essay: context on any academic or personal concerns; bullet points acceptable.", "limit": "500 words max", "required": false}], "source_url": "https://academics.business.columbia.edu/mba/admissions/application-requirements"}, "video_assessment": null, "interview": {"value": "By invitation only, cannot be requested; usually with an alumni interviewer in the applicant''s geographic area; conducted in English. Decision aimed within two weeks of interview report.", "source_url": "https://academics.business.columbia.edu/mba/admissions/application-requirements"}, "recommendations": {"value": "One recommendation for first-time applicants, ideally current supervisor (if 6+ months full-time work); former direct supervisor or senior professional associate also acceptable. Up to 1,000 words; applicant must not draft it. Must arrive within one week of submission.", "source_url": "https://academics.business.columbia.edu/mba/admissions/application-requirements"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Bachelor''s degree or equivalent; upload transcripts from every institution (official digitally encrypted copies if admitted); resume/CV (1 page ideal, 2 max); GPA as on transcript; academic integrity rules (generative AI only for brainstorming/editing).", "source_url": "https://academics.business.columbia.edu/admissions/mba/application-requirements"}, "notes": "Non-English transcripts and recommendations must be translated/transcribed by an official notarized agency; WES evaluation not required; you may translate your own transcripts but not your own recommendation. Financial guarantee statement optional at application but required for I-20. Essay prompts below come from the /mba/admissions/ page, which does