online application.", "source_url": "https://academics.business.columbia.edu/msm/admissions/application-requirements"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Resume/CV; transcripts from all post-secondary institutions (unofficial upload first; official if admitted). Typical student has coursework in probability/statistics and linear algebra; Python or R programming desirable; all majors welcome, STEM encouraged.", "source_url": "https://academics.business.columbia.edu/msm/admissions/application-requirements"}, "notes": "Non-English transcripts/letters must be professionally transcribed and notarized; WES evaluation not required. 2026-27 deadlines not found: the program admissions pages read were stale (2024 deadline passed, Fall 2025 entry) and the deadlines page failed to load. Duration from the /ms listing. Three-year degrees reviewed case by case."}'::jsonb,'{"class_label": "Class entering 2025", "gmat_avg": null, "gmat_median": null, "gmat_range": null, "gmat_focus_median": null, "gmat_focus_range": null, "gre_verbal_avg": 160, "gre_quant_avg": 168, "gre_range": "Verbal 143-170, Quant 159-170 (range as published, percentile basis not stated)", "gpa_avg": 3.8, "gpa_range": null, "work_exp_avg_years": 3.58, "work_exp_range": null, "class_size": 48, "international_pct": null, "women_pct": 77, "countries": 13, "pct_submitted_gre": null, "source_url": "https://academics.business.columbia.edu/admissions/ms/class-profiles", "source_name": "Columbia Business School MS class profiles"}'::jsonb,'{"report_label": "Class of 2024 (26 graduates)", "employed_3_months_pct": null, "median_base_salary": null, "mean_base_salary": null, "top_industries": "Consulting (Data/AI), Advertising, FinTech, Media & Entertainment, Technology, Retail & Luxury", "top_employers": "Apple, TikTok, Uber, Dentsu, Van Cleef & Arpels", "international_employed_note": "12 full-time + 2 internship offers; 8 no recent info. US 11, Mainland China 3 (table ambiguous). No salary reported.", "source_url": "https://academics.business.columbia.edu/sites/academics/files-efs/imce-uploads/MSM/MSM-2024-Employment-Report.pdf", "source_name": "CBS MSM 2024 Employment Report"}'::jsonb),
('Berkeley Haas','Full-Time MBA','mba','full-time','21 months','Fall 2027','https://mba.haas.berkeley.edu/','{"deadlines": {"value": "2026-27 cycle: Round 1 Sept 10, 2026 (decision Dec 10, 2026); Round 2 Jan 7, 2027 (decision Mar 25, 2027); Round 3 Apr 1, 2027 (decision May 6, 2027).", "source_url": "https://mba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/"}, "application_fee": null, "tests": {"value": "GMAT or GRE required, no minimum, no preference; highest cumulative score considered; must be taken on or before the round deadline. Waiver policy not stated on pages read.", "source_url": "https://mba.haas.berkeley.edu/hubfs/FT/App%20Bootcamp/Application_Checklist.pdf?hsLang=en-us"}, "english": {"ielts_min": "7.0 overall, 6.5 speaking and writing (IELTS Academic)", "toefl_min": "5 on the 6.0 scale, speaking and writing 4.5; former scale: 90 iBT", "duolingo": "not stated", "pte_min": null, "other_tests": null, "waiver": "Exempt if degree is from an institution in a country where English is the primary official language, or you completed 1+ year full-time coursework with B or better at a university in US, UK, Australia, English-speaking Canada or Singapore. For Fall 2027 only scores from tests on/after June 1, 2025.", "source_url": "https://mba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/language-proficiency-requirements"}, "essays": {"items": [{"prompt": "What are your short-term and long-term career goals, and how will an MBA from Haas help you achieve those goals?", "limit": "300 words", "required": true}, {"prompt": "Supplemental information: explain the ''distance traveled'' in your personal and professional journey, how your background shaped your perspectives and decisions.", "limit": "300 words", "required": true}, {"prompt": "Optional essays: explain hardships/unusual circumstances or gaps (employment breaks, academic irregularities).", "limit": "not stated", "required": false}], "source_url": "https://mba.haas.berkeley.edu/hubfs/FT/App%20Bootcamp/Application_Checklist.pdf?hsLang=en-us"}, "video_assessment": {"value": "Video essay, 2 minutes max: ''What makes you feel alive when you are doing it, and why.''", "source_url": "https://mba.haas.berkeley.edu/hubfs/FT/App%20Bootcamp/Application_Checklist.pdf?hsLang=en-us"}, "interview": {"value": "By invitation only, rolling. Either a prerecorded video session or a live remote conversation with a current student or alum; no in-person option described.", "source_url": "https://mba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/interview"}, "recommendations": {"value": "Two letters; at least one from a current or former employer (explain if not possible). Give recommenders 4+ weeks; do not write your own.", "source_url": "https://mba.haas.berkeley.edu/hubfs/FT/App%20Bootcamp/Application_Checklist.pdf?hsLang=en-us"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Resume (1 page recommended); work experience history; list up to 5 extracurricular activities; transcripts from every degree-granting institution since high school; optional background questions.", "source_url": "https://mba.haas.berkeley.edu/hubfs/FT/App%20Bootcamp/Application_Checklist.pdf?hsLang=en-us"}, "notes": "Application fee amount not found on pages read. The checklist PDF is undated, so essay prompts may reflect a prior cycle; confirm in the application. Non-US degrees: diploma copy plus certified English translations (ATA, Ministry of Education, or WES ICAP); minimum a 4-year bachelor''s or a master''s completed two years after a bachelor''s (source https://mba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/academic-records). Duolingo/PTE not mentioned on the English page: do not assume accepted."}'::jsonb,'{"class_label": "MBA Class of 2027 (Class of 2028 not found on official page); median and middle-80% only, no averages", "gmat_avg": null, "gmat_median": 730, "gmat_range": "middle 80%: 669-767 (GMAT Classic)", "gmat_focus_median": 675, "gmat_focus_range": "middle 80%: 637-725 (GMAT Focus)", "gre_verbal_avg": null, "gre_quant_avg": null, "gre_range": "Verbal median 161 (middle 80% 155-167); Quant median 162 (middle 80% 155-169)", "gpa_avg": 3.67, "gpa_range": "middle 80%: 3.4-3.91", "work_exp_avg_years": 5.6, "work_exp_range": "middle 80%: 3.2-8.2 years", "class_size": 273, "international_pct": 44, "women_pct": 43, "countries": 42, "pct_submitted_gre": null, "source_url": "https://mba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/class-profile", "source_name": "Berkeley Haas official MBA class profile"}'::jsonb,'{"report_label": "Class of 2025", "employed_3_months_pct": 84, "median_base_salary": "USD 167,250", "mean_base_salary": "USD 164,930", "top_industries": "Tech/telecom 38.6%, Consulting 26.8%, Financial services 15.7%, Energy 5.2%, Healthcare 3.3%", "top_employers": "Adobe, Amazon, Deloitte, McKinsey, Nvidia", "international_employed_note": "86% of seekers had offers and 84% accepted at 3 months (employed_3_months_pct = accepted). Nearly 97% of employed grads stayed in US. No visa info.", "source_url": "https://www.clearadmit.com/2025/12/berkeley-haas-mba-class-of-2025-employment-report/", "source_name": "Clear Admit summary; Haas newsroom https://newsroom.haas.berkeley.edu/record-high-starting-compensation-for-2025-ftmba-grads-fueled-by-tech-sector-rebound/"}'::jsonb),
('Berkeley Haas','Evening & Weekend MBA','mba','part-time','3 years','2026-27 cycle (term not named on page; tests page references Fall 2027)','https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/','{"deadlines": {"value": "2026-27 cycle: Round 1 Nov 5, 2026 (decision Dec 7, 2026); Round 2 Jan 14, 2027 (decision Mar 9, 2027); Round 3 Mar 29, 2027 (decision May 14, 2027). Due 11:59 PM Pacific.", "source_url": "https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions"}, "application_fee": {"value": "USD 200 non-refundable; waivers for nonprofit/public service, US military, African-continent citizens, reapplicants within two years, others.", "source_url": "https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/application"}, "tests": {"value": "GMAT, GRE or EA required unless waived (US Business/Economics/STEM degree with GPA 3.4+, STEM PhD or listed doctoral medical degree, UC Berkeley alumni with quantitative essay). No minimum score. Scores on/after Oct 1, 2021 for Fall 2027.", "source_url": "https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/part-time-mba-gmat"}, "english": {"ielts_min": null, "toefl_min": null, "duolingo": "not stated", "pte_min": null, "other_tests": "TOEFL or IELTS required (page mentions only these two)", "waiver": "Required if undergraduate degree is from outside the U.S., UK, Australia, English-speaking Canada or Singapore. Waived if, at time of application, you completed at least one year of full-time academic coursework with grades of B or better at a recognized U.S. institution (ESL, non-English instruction, courses completed after applying, non-degree/non-academic courses do not count). Tests taken before June 2025 not accepted. Page lists no minimum scores.", "source_url": "https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/application"}, "essays": {"items": [{"prompt": "Personal Story: Tell us what makes you feel alive when you are doing it, and why? (also something not evident elsewhere in your application)", "limit": "300 words ideal, up to 400", "required": true}, {"prompt": "Professional Statement: why you are seeking a Haas MBA now; short- and long-term career objectives.", "limit": "200 words max", "required": true}], "source_url": "https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/application"}, "video_assessment": {"value": "Video interview: two short questions (one on desire to attend Haas, one to get to know you), 1-2 minutes each; 7 days from receiving link.", "source_url": "https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/application"}, "interview": {"value": "Video interview as above; no live interview described on the page.", "source_url": "https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/application"}, "recommendations": {"value": "One letter on management and leadership potential; current direct supervisor recommended, not required.", "source_url": "https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/application"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Resume 1-2 pages PDF; list each professional role since undergraduate studies.", "source_url": "https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/application"}, "notes": "Program does not assist with student visas; students usually rely on employers (L1, H1B), per https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/part-time-mba-international-applicants. Duration from https://haas.berkeley.edu/programs/. Transcript rules: https://ewmba.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/transcripts not fetched."}'::jsonb,null,null),
('Berkeley Haas','Master of Financial Engineering (MFE)','masters','full-time','One year full-time (two-year Flex option for students who keep working)','Spring 2028','https://mfe.haas.berkeley.edu/','{"deadlines": {"value": "Spring 2028 cycle (9:00 a.m. ET): Round 1 Dec 1, 2026; Round 2 Jan 27, 2027; Round 3 Apr 1, 2027; Round 4 Jul 1, 2027; late applications until Jul 15, 2027 space permitting. Decisions ~9 weeks after submission.", "source_url": "https://mfe.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions"}, "application_fee": null, "tests": {"value": "GRE/GMAT required though some applicants can waive; can apply with a future test date. From the Spring 2026 cycle blog post, current policy not confirmed.", "source_url": "https://blogs.haas.berkeley.edu/mfe/your-quick-guide-to-the-uc-berkeley-haas-mfe-application"}, "english": null, "essays": {"items": [], "source_url": "https://blogs.haas.berkeley.edu/mfe/your-quick-guide-to-the-uc-berkeley-haas-mfe-application"}, "video_assessment": {"value": "Video essay required (Spring 2026 cycle blog post).", "source_url": "https://blogs.haas.berkeley.edu/mfe/your-quick-guide-to-the-uc-berkeley-haas-mfe-application"}, "interview": {"value": "One-on-one with MFE alumni; tests problem solving, quantitative reasoning, coding (Python/C++ recommended), communication (Spring 2026 cycle blog post).", "source_url": "https://blogs.haas.berkeley.edu/mfe/your-quick-guide-to-the-uc-berkeley-haas-mfe-application"}, "recommendations": {"value": "Two letters of recommendation (Spring 2026 cycle blog post).", "source_url": "https://blogs.haas.berkeley.edu/mfe/your-quick-guide-to-the-uc-berkeley-haas-mfe-application"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Experience in programming (C++, Python), statistics/econometrics, machine learning; post-university work experience preferred, not required; prerequisite courses (B or higher) may be completed with a plan before the program: calculus, linear algebra, PDEs, statistics, numerical analysis, finance, English writing.", "source_url": "https://mfe.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/prerequisites"}, "notes": "The MFE requirements page loads with collapsed sections, so fee, test waivers, English minimums and essay prompts could not be read; the international page held only placeholder text. Items sourced from the blog describe the Spring 2026 cycle. Duration/intake from the admissions page."}'::jsonb,'{"class_label": "Class entering 2025", "gmat_avg": null, "gmat_median": null, "gmat_range": null, "gmat_focus_median": null, "gmat_focus_range": null, "gre_verbal_avg": null, "gre_quant_avg": null, "gre_range": "Average percentiles only: Quant 91st, Verbal 79th", "gpa_avg": null, "gpa_range": null, "work_exp_avg_years": 2.47, "work_exp_range": null, "class_size": 84, "international_pct": null, "women_pct": 30, "countries": 11, "pct_submitted_gre": null, "source_url": "https://mfe.haas.berkeley.edu/admissions/class-profile", "source_name": "Haas MFE class profile"}'::jsonb,'{"report_label": "Class of 2025 (70 seeking, 67 accepted)", "employed_3_months_pct": null, "median_base_salary": "USD 150,000", "mean_base_salary": "USD 148,318", "top_industries": "Function: portfolio mgmt/quant research 55%, trading 12%, strats/structuring 10%", "top_employers": null, "international_employed_note": "13% placed internationally (2025); locations: US East Coast 60%, other US 13%, CA 10%, Chicago 5%. Mean signing bonus USD 34,267. 3-month % not stated for 2025.", "source_url": "https://mfe.haas.berkeley.edu/careers/mfe-placements", "source_name": "Haas MFE employment report"}'::jsonb),
('Yale SOM','MBA (full-time, in-residence)','mba','full-time','2 years','Fall 2027 (2026-27 application cycle)','https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba','{"deadlines": {"value": "2026-27 cycle: Round 1 Sep 15, 2026 (decision Dec 3, 2026); Round 2 Jan 6, 2027 (decision Mar 18, 2027); Round 3 Apr 7, 2027 (decision May 13, 2027). Also accepts Consortium and QuestBridge applications on their own deadlines.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information"}, "application_fee": {"value": "USD 250 standard; USD 175 if annual compensation under USD 50,000; USD 125 if under USD 25,000. Compensation is verified on enrollment. Waivers for groups such as US military, Peace Corps, QuestBridge, qualifying US colleges (request at least 48 hours before deadline).", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/FAQ"}, "tests": {"value": "GMAT or GRE required (current and past versions, online and shorter versions accepted); LSAT accepted for those considering law school. Test requirement is not waived for any applicant. No minimum score. Scores valid 5 years. Official scores due by the post-submission materials deadline. Superscores considered if reported. Executive Assessment not mentioned.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/FAQ"}, "english": {"ielts_min": null, "toefl_min": null, "duolingo": "not stated", "pte_min": null, "other_tests": null, "waiver": "No minimum scores: the FAQ states the TOEFL, PTE Academic, or IELTS exam is not required for international applicants. Fluency in English is required for admission. Non-English transcripts need original plus notarized English translation.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/faq"}, "essays": {"items": [{"prompt": "Choose one: (1) Describe the biggest commitment you have ever made. (2) Describe the community that has been most meaningful to you. (3) Describe the most significant challenge you have faced.", "limit": "500 words", "required": true}], "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/application-guide"}, "video_assessment": {"value": "Two pre-recorded video questions, 60 seconds to respond to each, completed after submitting the application and paying the fee. Used with a light touch; no AI or scripts.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/application-guide"}, "interview": {"value": "By invitation only, rolling within each round. 30 minutes, conducted by a current second-year student, recent alum, or Admissions Committee member. Blind interview (interviewer sees only the resume).", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/application-guide"}, "recommendations": {"value": "Two professional recommendations; one ideally from a current supervisor. Recommenders should be senior to applicant. Letters may be in English or native language with translation.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/application-guide"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Resume (one page unless more than 10 years of work). Unofficial transcripts for all undergraduate and graduate coursework (official only on enrollment). Online ETS Behavioral Assessment (about 25 min). Explain employment gaps over 3 months and career transitions. Up to two activities per timeframe.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/application-guide"}, "notes": "Non-English transcripts need translation (notarized if the school provides none), plus a copy of the original. Three-year degrees from accredited institutions may apply. Credential evaluation service not mentioned. Visa and financing details come after admission; no document list published on the pages read."}'::jsonb,'{"class_label": "Class of 2027 (entered fall 2025; Class of 2028 profile not yet published, Yale story says it will be shared once finalized)", "gmat_avg": null, "gmat_median": 740, "gmat_range": "80% range: 691-760 (GMAT Classic)", "gmat_focus_median": 675, "gmat_focus_range": "80% range: 638-715", "gre_verbal_avg": null, "gre_quant_avg": null, "gre_range": "Verbal median 163 (80% range 158-169); Quant median 166 (80% range 160-170)", "gpa_avg": null, "gpa_range": "median 3.69; 80% range 3.37-3.93 (US schools, 4.0 scale)", "work_exp_avg_years": 5, "work_exp_range": null, "class_size": 367, "international_pct": 41, "women_pct": 44, "countries": 47, "pct_submitted_gre": 47, "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/index%2Ephp/programs/mba/admissions/class-profile", "source_name": "Yale SOM MBA class profile page"}'::jsonb,'{"report_label": "Employment Report 2025-26 (full-time MBA, Class of 2025); figure below is share with job OFFERS within 3 months (accepted: 79.9%, per Poets&Quants)", "employed_3_months_pct": 82.1, "median_base_salary": "USD 175,000 (25th pct 140,000; 75th pct 190,000)", "mean_base_salary": null, "top_industries": "Consulting 36.7%, Finance 28.9% (investment banking 17.9%), Technology 8.3%, Healthcare/Pharma 5.0% (share of job seekers, per Poets&Quants)", "top_employers": "Amazon, Bain, Bank of America, Barclays, BCG, Citi, Deloitte Consulting, EY-Parthenon, IBM, JPMorgan Chase, McKinsey, Microsoft, Goldman Sachs (121 unique employers)", "international_employed_note": "International roles were 7.2% of full-time employment (median base USD 120K); international students'' 25th pct base USD 133,200 vs US 140,000; Asia 66.7% of non-US hires. No visa sponsorship rate given.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/index%2Ephp/programs/mba/career-paths/employment-report-2025-26", "source_name": "Yale SOM Employment Report 2025-26; industry split from Poets&Quants 2025-12-15"}'::jsonb),
('Yale SOM','MBA Silver Scholars (accelerated path for college seniors)','mba','full-time','Not stated (Yale core year, then 1+ years of full-time work, then final year of electives)','2026-27 cycle (exact entry term not stated)','https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/silver-scholars','{"deadlines": {"value": "2026-27 cycle: Round 1 Sep 15, 2026; Round 2 Jan 6, 2027; Round 3 Apr 7, 2027.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/silver-scholars"}, "application_fee": {"value": "Standard fee USD 250 (MBA application, same one Silver Scholars complete); sliding scale USD 175 (earning under USD 50,000) and USD 125 (under USD 25,000); fee waivers available by request at least 48 hours before deadline. Cycle 2026-27.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/faq"}, "tests": {"value": "GMAT or GRE accepted (including online and shorter versions); LSAT accepted from candidates who have considered or are considering law school. No baseline or minimum scores. Official score reports required. Silver Scholars use the same application as the full-time MBA. Cycle 2026-27.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/application-guide"}, "english": {"ielts_min": null, "toefl_min": null, "duolingo": "not stated", "pte_min": null, "other_tests": null, "waiver": "No minimum scores: TOEFL, PTE Academic, or IELTS not required for international applicants; fluency in English required. Silver Scholars complete the same application as the full-time MBA.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/faq"}, "essays": {"items": [{"prompt": "Choose one: (1) Describe the biggest commitment you have ever made. (2) Describe the community that has been most meaningful to you. (3) Describe the most significant challenge you have faced.", "limit": "500 words (limit, not necessarily the goal)", "required": true}], "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/application-guide"}, "video_assessment": {"value": "Two previously recorded video questions asked by admissions team members; 60 seconds to respond to each; completed after submitting the application and paying the fee (2026-27 application guide).", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/application-guide"}, "interview": {"value": "If invited, half-hour interview with one or two Silver Scholars Committee members covering academic and professional experiences and career aspirations.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/silver-scholars"}, "recommendations": {"value": "Two letters: one academic (instructor or advisor) and one from an employer supervisor (or extracurricular/volunteer organization if no work experience).", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/application-information/application-guide"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Eligibility: mainly college seniors with degree conferred Aug 1, 2026 to Jul 31, 2027; extensive full-time work or over 2 years military service generally disqualifies. Uses the same online application as the full-time MBA.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mba/admissions/silver-scholars"}, "notes": "Fee, tests, English and essays not stated on the Silver Scholars page; it says applicants complete the same application as full-time MBA (see MBA entry). Likely not relevant for an applicant with 5+ years of work experience."}'::jsonb,null,null),
('Yale SOM','Master of Advanced Management (MAM)','masters','full-time','1 year','Class of 2028 (2026-27 cycle; start month not stated)','https://som.yale.edu/programs/mam','{"deadlines": {"value": "Class of 2028: opens Sep 1, 2026. Round 1 Dec 1, 2026 (Global Network schools only; decision Jan 8, 2027); Round 2 Jan 12, 2027 (Feb 12); Round 3 Feb 23, 2027 (Mar 25); Round 4 Mar 30, 2027 (Apr 29).", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mam/admissions/application-information"}, "application_fee": {"value": "USD 95, non-refundable, paid online by credit card after submitting the complete application.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mam/admissions/application-information"}, "tests": {"value": "GMAT or GRE accepted (online versions too); official report required; no minimum score.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mam/admissions/application-information"}, "english": null, "essays": {"items": [], "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mam/admissions/application-information"}, "video_assessment": {"value": "Video questions required; available within 24 hours of paying and submitting. Not meant to be difficult.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mam/admissions/application-information"}, "interview": {"value": "Zoom interview with the Office of Admissions for successful candidates after round review.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mam/admissions/application-information"}, "recommendations": {"value": "One professional recommendation from a professional email (no Gmail/Yahoo) plus a confirmation letter from the Dean/Director of the MBA program stating good standing.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mam/admissions/application-information"}, "other_requirements": {"value": "Must hold or be completing an MBA or equivalent. Transcripts from all programs including the MBA (unofficial to apply, official to enroll). One-page resume recommended.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mam/admissions/application-information"}, "notes": "For MBA graduates only, so not an entry route for Octavia''s first-year MBA. Four essays of 300 words or fewer each; prompts not listed on the page. Non-English transcripts need translation. Visa needed for non-US citizens; USD 3,000 non-refundable deposit on admission. English test rules not stated on this page."}'::jsonb,null,'{"report_label": "Class of 2025 employment report; 96.2% received a job offer by 6 months (not 3 months), 74.4% survey response", "employed_3_months_pct": null, "median_base_salary": null, "mean_base_salary": null, "top_industries": null, "top_employers": "Cumulative list (not Class of 2025 only) includes Bain, BCG, McKinsey, Google, Microsoft, JPMorgan Chase, Amazon", "international_employed_note": "71.4% of hires in the US (52.4% Northeast), 9.5% Europe, 4.8% each Asia, MENA, Canada, South America. No salary data. MAM is for students who already hold an MBA/graduate business degree, so it is not pre-experience.", "source_url": "https://som.yale.edu/programs/mam/careers/employment-report-2025", "source_name": "Yale SOM MAM employment report Class of 2025"}'::jsonb),
