-tops-destination-2025-oxford-mfe-graduates-and-95-have-secured-new-jobs-report", "source_name": "Oxford Saïd news: 2025 MFE graduates (average age 23)"}'::jsonb,'{"report_label": "MSc Financial Economics class of 2025 (news summary; full 2025 report PDF not fetched). Earlier: Class of 2022/23 report", "employed_3_months_pct": null, "median_base_salary": null, "mean_base_salary": "2025: average above GBP 64k (highest UK finance over GBP 120k). 2022/23: mean GBP 60,578 (finance 66,761; consulting 53,547)", "top_industries": "2025: Finance 82%, Consulting 11%. 2022/23: Finance 70%, Consulting 25%, Other 5%", "top_employers": "2025: Barclays, Blackstone, Goldman Sachs, HSBC, JP Morgan, Morgan Stanley, UBS", "international_employed_note": "2025: 95% secured new roles within SIX months (not 3). Graduates joined orgs in 12 countries; London 35%, Hong Kong 15%, North America 11%. 2022/23: 92% accepted job within 6 months, 99% international, 21 nationalities, 56% women.", "source_url": "https://www.sbs.ox.ac.uk/news/finance-tops-destination-2025-oxford-mfe-graduates-and-95-have-secured-new-jobs-report", "source_name": "Oxford Saïd news 2025; 2022/23 figures from https://www.sbs.ox.ac.uk/sites/default/files/2024-05/MFE-Employment-Report-2024.pdf"}'::jsonb),
